      "title": "SC to hear bail pleas of Umar Khalid, Sharjeel Imam in Delhi riots case",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/sc-to-hear-bail-pleas-of-umar-khalid-sharjeel-imam-in-delhi-riots-case-126112400249_1.html",
      "description": "The Supreme Court is slated to hear on Wednesday pleas of activists Sharjeel Imam and Umar Khalid challenging a Delhi High Court order denying them bail in an Unlawful Activities (Prevention) Act (UAPA) case related to the alleged \"larger conspiracy\" behind the February 2020 northeast Delhi riots.\nAs per the cause list, a bench comprising Chief Justice Surya Kant and Justices Joymalya Bagchi and V Mohana is likely to hear the matter.\nIn their pleas before the top court, the activists have sought bail, contending that the prosecution has failed to examine protected witnesses and the one-year embargo imposed by the Supreme Court is nearing its expiry.\nThe petition by Imam contended that the chargesheet was filed on September 25, 2020, in which 18 accused face trial and the prosecution has cited more than 900 witnesses, including 47 protected witnesses.\nKhalid, in his plea, also cited the failure to examine protected witnesses and said the expiry of the one-year embargo would mean tha",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-24T05:33:59"
    }
